{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"code\":\"    def should_refresh_early(\\n        self,\\n        time_remaining: float,\\n        ttl: float,\\n        key_name: str = \\\"unknown\\\",\\n    ) -> bool:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Return True when the entry should be refreshed before expiry.\\n\\n        BUG_55: the ratio comparison is inverted, causing early refreshes\\n        when the entry is FAR from expiry (most of the TTL left) rather\\n        than CLOSE to expiry (little TTL left).\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if ttl <= 0:\\n            return False\\n\\n        ratio = time_remaining / ttl\\n\\n        if ratio < self.threshold:\\n            from cache.metrics import metrics\\n\\n            metrics.increment(\\\"cache.stampede.prevented\\\")\\n            self.refreshes_triggered += 1\\n            return True\\n\\n        return False\\n\",\"comments\":\"Flip the threshold comparison so refreshes happen near expiration and emit the cache.stampede.prevented metric when the guard triggers.\"}"}}
